## **Step 6: Automatically identify which files you changed**

Once you complete the manual review, execute:

```
while read -r pipeline
do
    if cmp -s \
        "dev-pipelines/$pipeline.conf" \
        "manual-review-pipelines/$pipeline.conf"
    then
        echo "$pipeline : NO_CHANGE"
    else
        echo "$pipeline : MODIFIED"
    fi
done < manual-review.txt
```

This identifies which working configurations have changed compared with the original Non-LMA configurations.

## **Step 7: Copy only the modified and reviewed pipelines**

After reviewing and approving the changes, execute:

```
while read -r pipeline
do
    if ! cmp -s \
        "dev-pipelines/$pipeline.conf" \
        "manual-review-pipelines/$pipeline.conf"
    then
        cp -i "manual-review-pipelines/$pipeline.conf" \
        "updated-dev-pipelines/$pipeline.conf"

        echo "Processed: $pipeline"
    fi
done < manual-review.txt
```

The `-i` option asks before overwriting an existing working file.

